1
00:00:06,260 --> 00:00:09,550
Nice, Sumi-chan! Up high!

2
00:00:09,550 --> 00:00:11,280
That was fun.

3
00:00:15,290 --> 00:00:18,170
Don't forget the kissy face, Sumi-chan!

4
00:00:59,660 --> 00:01:01,370
I thought I was good at going it alone

5
00:00:59,660 --> 00:01:01,370
Would you prefer to go together?

6
00:01:28,190 --> 00:01:28,900
Place
your finger here

7
00:01:46,960 --> 00:01:50,040
Rent-a-Girlfriend

8
00:01:52,260 --> 00:01:56,680
"Long Time No Girlfriend"

9
00:02:02,810 --> 00:02:06,000
Gah, I can't! It's been two days 
since we got back to Tokyo,

10
00:02:06,000 --> 00:02:09,650
and I keep thinking about that kiss, 
all day and all night!

11
00:02:06,250 --> 00:02:09,650
This has to be
some kind of curse!!

12
00:02:09,990 --> 00:02:13,120
My world's been dyed pink ever since.

13
00:02:12,780 --> 00:02:16,240
dazed

14
00:02:13,120 --> 00:02:16,240
My brain must be completely broken.

15
00:02:16,670 --> 00:02:18,870
It not like that was 
the first time, right?

16
00:02:19,140 --> 00:02:22,370
<i>Mizuhara and I actually kissed.</i>

17
00:02:22,660 --> 00:02:25,880
<i>You could write off the first time as CPR.</i>

18
00:02:25,880 --> 00:02:27,290
<i>But this was totally a kiss.</i>

19
00:02:27,290 --> 00:02:30,960
<i>Kiss is. Kiss is in-itself. 
Kiss is what it is.</i>

20
00:02:30,960 --> 00:02:32,420
Not again!

21
00:02:31,760 --> 00:02:35,220
Embrace the kiss

22
00:02:32,420 --> 00:02:35,560
I can't eat or do my assignments!

23
00:02:35,220 --> 00:02:37,720
The hard disk of my brain is being overwritten bit by bit!

24
00:02:35,560 --> 00:02:38,400
Am I gonna be like this 
for the rest of my life?!

25
00:02:38,400 --> 00:02:39,630
Wait, calm down.

26
00:02:39,220 --> 00:02:43,430
Don't trip out

27
00:02:39,220 --> 00:02:43,430
again!!

28
00:02:39,630 --> 00:02:43,430
You also put her on the spot. 
Settle down and think this through.

29
00:02:43,790 --> 00:02:45,980
Hear me out, Mizuhara!

30
00:02:46,310 --> 00:02:47,280
I'm sorry.

31
00:02:47,940 --> 00:02:51,060
<i>She knew I was gonna ask her out, right?</i>

32
00:02:51,060 --> 00:02:55,420
<i>Still... she kissed me! To help me out.</i>

33
00:02:55,420 --> 00:02:57,190
<i>That's like...</i>

34
00:02:55,750 --> 00:03:00,160
Mm

35
00:02:55,750 --> 00:03:00,160
Mm

36
00:02:55,750 --> 00:03:00,160
Smooch

37
00:02:55,750 --> 00:03:00,160
Mm

38
00:02:57,190 --> 00:02:58,570
<i>I love you, too!</i>

39
00:02:58,570 --> 00:03:00,160
<i>That's like giving me the green light!</i>

40
00:03:00,160 --> 00:03:01,870
The eyes of a shoplifter

41
00:03:00,160 --> 00:03:01,870
No, wait!

42
00:03:01,870 --> 00:03:06,580
Did she really know? There's a chance she 
didn't catch on to what I was gonna do!

43
00:03:06,580 --> 00:03:11,380
That'd mean she really did help me 
out of the goodness of her heart!

44
00:03:08,080 --> 00:03:10,840
And what she said
after that was true

45
00:03:11,380 --> 00:03:14,300
<i>Who are you telling to wait over and over?</i>

46
00:03:11,590 --> 00:03:14,300
Kindness

47
00:03:14,600 --> 00:03:17,810
But remember, she asked if I was trying 
to pop some kind of question!

48
00:03:17,810 --> 00:03:19,410
What else could she have meant there?

49
00:03:19,410 --> 00:03:23,520
Is there some other kind of question 
to pop that I'm simply not aware of?

50
00:03:21,060 --> 00:03:23,520
guy girl the talk

51
00:03:21,060 --> 00:03:23,520
The merits of working up the courage to pop the question

52
00:03:23,820 --> 00:03:26,980
I figured not. It had to be 
about me asking her out, right?

53
00:03:28,230 --> 00:03:31,800
But it's hard to tell what goes 
through Mizuhara's head sometimes!

54
00:03:31,800 --> 00:03:34,040
Wait, what? Where did all this come from?

55
00:03:34,040 --> 00:03:35,920
I seriously can't believe you.

56
00:03:35,920 --> 00:03:38,180
What if I try to ask her out again,

57
00:03:36,610 --> 00:03:40,950
eek

58
00:03:38,180 --> 00:03:40,950
and she acts like it
came out of nowhere?

59
00:03:41,390 --> 00:03:44,120
Mizuhara's seriously an enigma.

60
00:03:41,870 --> 00:03:47,670
Love Neurosis

61
00:03:44,120 --> 00:03:47,670
Gimme a top-secret gadget 
that lets me read her mind.

62
00:03:47,920 --> 00:03:51,290
<i>Even after we split off from 
the group at Ueno Station...</i>

63
00:03:52,260 --> 00:03:54,640
I need to stop by somewhere.

64
00:03:53,340 --> 00:03:55,260
I'll take a different route home

65
00:03:55,620 --> 00:03:56,720
See you.

66
00:03:56,990 --> 00:03:58,340
S-Sure.

67
00:04:01,230 --> 00:04:03,390
R-Ruka-chan?!

68
00:04:01,690 --> 00:04:03,390
Hey, that hurt.

69
00:04:03,730 --> 00:04:07,140
You deserve to feel at least 1% 
of the pain you put me through!

70
00:04:05,430 --> 00:04:07,140
Also, get away
from him!!

71
00:04:07,470 --> 00:04:11,030
Listen, I'll say what happened 
this time doesn't count.

72
00:04:10,730 --> 00:04:13,190
The most special
of exceptions!!

73
00:04:11,030 --> 00:04:14,610
That it was a necessary evil to 
protect my boyfriend's reputation.

74
00:04:14,610 --> 00:04:17,440
But you need to remember where you stand!

75
00:04:17,810 --> 00:04:20,020
You're a rental girlfriend.

76
00:04:20,020 --> 00:04:22,700
You shouldn't be getting 
on any trains with a client.

77
00:04:23,180 --> 00:04:25,250
Wait, Ruka-chan. 
I'm the one to blame here.

78
00:04:25,250 --> 00:04:26,950
You're not off the hook either!

79
00:04:25,490 --> 00:04:31,880
nag nag

80
00:04:26,950 --> 00:04:30,560
You got a golden opportunity to 
come clean, and you just wasted it!

81
00:04:30,560 --> 00:04:32,630
Do you realize that?!

82
00:04:32,630 --> 00:04:34,500
I wouldn't call it "golden."

83
00:04:34,500 --> 00:04:35,840
But that's what it was!

84
00:04:36,140 --> 00:04:37,070
Sorry.

85
00:04:38,240 --> 00:04:39,760
I'm kind of in a hurry.

86
00:04:45,720 --> 00:04:50,850
Heck, she was
even kinda standoffish

87
00:04:45,930 --> 00:04:50,850
<i>Ruka-chan's alarm bells were going off, 
but Mizuhara was just acting normal.</i>

88
00:04:51,140 --> 00:04:54,960
How could she stay so calm 
after all that happened?

89
00:04:55,550 --> 00:04:58,240
Does she have ice in 
her veins or something?

90
00:04:58,240 --> 00:05:00,700
That was a <i>kiss</i>! She <i>kissed</i> you, dude!

91
00:05:01,270 --> 00:05:02,840
<i>But he was right.</i>

92
00:05:02,840 --> 00:05:04,960
<i>You can make all the excuses 
for it you want,</i>

93
00:05:04,960 --> 00:05:08,160
<i>but going back to normal after that 
just doesn't make any sense at all.</i>

94
00:05:08,460 --> 00:05:12,620
<i>Besides, I'm this close to going insane. 
It's not about logic or reason anymore.</i>

95
00:05:13,120 --> 00:05:16,080
<i>Tell me, Mizuhara. 
How do you feel about everything?</i>

96
00:05:16,080 --> 00:05:19,880
<i>Was that kiss purely to help me out? 
Nothing more than that?</i>

97
00:05:20,300 --> 00:05:24,040
<i>I wanna see her. I wanna see 
her face. I wanna hear her voice.</i>

98
00:05:24,460 --> 00:05:27,100
<i>I can't control myself anymore.</i>

99
00:05:28,050 --> 00:05:31,190
<i>She can't be in class this early.</i>

100
00:05:34,610 --> 00:05:36,270
Yoga
Free Trial!!

101
00:05:36,570 --> 00:05:41,030
Saved this mistakenly
delivered mail for
a time like this

102
00:05:37,080 --> 00:05:41,030
<i>I firmly believe we are in need of 
conversation at this moment!</i>

103
00:05:41,030 --> 00:05:42,990
Ichinose

104
00:05:45,940 --> 00:05:47,060
<i>It's all good.</i>

105
00:05:47,060 --> 00:05:49,620
<i>Worst case, I just came 
to hand over the mail.</i>

106
00:05:49,620 --> 00:05:53,020
<i>And if she's in a good mood, 
I'll make some small talk...</i>

107
00:05:53,020 --> 00:05:56,260
<i>and then ask her if she 
wants to chat a little.</i>

108
00:05:56,260 --> 00:05:58,270
<i>Screw it!</i>

109
00:06:06,010 --> 00:06:07,050
No response?!

110
00:06:07,600 --> 00:06:10,520
tremble tremble

111
00:06:17,960 --> 00:06:19,520
<i>I don't hear a peep.</i>

112
00:06:19,520 --> 00:06:21,610
<i>Is she out this early?</i>

113
00:06:22,090 --> 00:06:25,700
<i>If she didn't want me calling on her, 
she'd just come out yelling at me.</i>

114
00:06:26,120 --> 00:06:28,280
I've been chasing
my own tail again

115
00:06:26,410 --> 00:06:28,280
Aw, man.

116
00:06:28,560 --> 00:06:29,790
She's out, huh?

117
00:06:37,630 --> 00:06:40,180
<i>Eh, whatever. I'll come back another time.</i>

118
00:06:42,950 --> 00:06:43,800
Huh?

119
00:06:47,070 --> 00:06:48,680
<i>I just heard something.</i>

120
00:06:49,140 --> 00:06:52,780
<i>Does that mean she's home? 
Then why isn't she responding?</i>

121
00:06:53,140 --> 00:06:55,320
<i>O-One more time.</i>

122
00:06:56,900 --> 00:06:59,570
Face naturally
turns into this

123
00:07:03,490 --> 00:07:07,990
Glaring match
with the doorknob

124
00:07:03,990 --> 00:07:07,990
<i>Why is she still not answering? 
I know I sensed her in there!</i>

125
00:07:07,990 --> 00:07:10,700
<i>Or was it just my imagination?</i>

126
00:07:13,010 --> 00:07:18,330
<i>I can't talk to her through the opening. 
That'd be a repeat of that one time.</i>

127
00:07:13,200 --> 00:07:15,120
A dark chapter
of his life

128
00:07:21,560 --> 00:07:24,010
<i>Yeah, let's just say 
I was imagining things.</i>

129
00:07:43,630 --> 00:07:45,080
Man...

130
00:07:46,270 --> 00:07:47,430
I can't take this.

131
00:07:48,780 --> 00:07:50,780
Yoga
Free Trial!!

132
00:07:50,060 --> 00:07:52,780
<i>Did I really just imagine that, though?</i>

133
00:07:52,780 --> 00:07:55,750
<i>I don't know why, 
but I feel like she's home.</i>

134
00:07:53,790 --> 00:07:58,750
I can feel
her in there

135
00:07:55,750 --> 00:07:58,750
<i>Even more so after hearing 
that noise back there.</i>

136
00:07:59,110 --> 00:08:02,910
<i>Why didn't she answer, then? 
That'd mean she faked not being home...</i>

137
00:08:02,910 --> 00:08:05,340
<i>Because she didn't want to see me.</i>

138
00:08:05,770 --> 00:08:07,670
<i>Wait, why?</i>

139
00:08:07,670 --> 00:08:12,140
doooom

140
00:08:07,970 --> 00:08:09,210
<i>Why would she do that?</i>

141
00:08:09,210 --> 00:08:12,140
<i>Did I do something to piss her off?</i>

142
00:08:12,780 --> 00:08:16,180
<i>There's only one thing I can think of 
after everything that happened.</i>

143
00:08:16,180 --> 00:08:18,340
<i>She's totally mad at me!</i>

144
00:08:18,340 --> 00:08:20,900
I even had to kiss you 
because of this mess you created!

145
00:08:20,900 --> 00:08:25,110
I'm taking legal action now, so just 
wait at home until you get served!

146
00:08:25,110 --> 00:08:28,650
<i>Argh! She was being all nice,</i>

147
00:08:25,650 --> 00:08:33,200
Duh! She had to
kiss a guy like me!!

148
00:08:28,650 --> 00:08:30,700
<i>but deep down, she hated it all!</i>

149
00:08:30,700 --> 00:08:33,200
<i>And she lied to me to get away from me!</i>

150
00:08:33,200 --> 00:08:35,910
<i>Did she wash her mouth 
out thoroughly later?</i>

151
00:08:34,240 --> 00:08:35,200
splash splash

152
00:08:35,910 --> 00:08:37,870
<i>Gah! I could die right now!</i>

153
00:08:36,200 --> 00:08:41,880
I could ascend
or descend!!

154
00:08:37,870 --> 00:08:41,880
<i>I could die internally from the guilt 
and the massive blow to my self-esteem!</i>

155
00:08:43,590 --> 00:08:44,630
<i>But..</i>

156
00:08:44,980 --> 00:08:45,920
<i>But...</i>

157
00:08:45,920 --> 00:08:47,130
<i>But!</i>

158
00:08:47,470 --> 00:08:50,220
<i>Mizuhara, I can't take this.</i>

159
00:08:50,220 --> 00:08:53,640
<i>Even if I know I'm being a bother, I'm in 
no state to give up on you anymore.</i>

160
00:09:00,010 --> 00:09:02,980
One message wouldn't be too weird, right?

161
00:09:05,690 --> 00:09:12,070
Heya! Some yoga pamphlet addressed to you got delivered
to me instead. Should I slip it through your mail slot?

162
00:09:05,990 --> 00:09:07,590
Keep it natural.

163
00:09:07,590 --> 00:09:12,070
I'm just sounding her out. It's not like 
I'm asking her on a date or anything.

164
00:09:07,730 --> 00:09:12,070
You keep using
the yoga thing!

165
00:09:12,760 --> 00:09:16,780
Actually, should I say 
"put" instead of "slip"?

166
00:09:16,780 --> 00:09:18,540
Phrasing is important.

167
00:09:18,540 --> 00:09:23,860
But should I avoid being too businesslike 
and keep it casual? Which is it?

168
00:09:21,590 --> 00:09:23,860
<i>The most irrelevant dilemma of all time!</i>

169
00:09:24,170 --> 00:09:27,420
<i>Would this be my first time texting 
her outside the movie thing?</i>

170
00:09:26,210 --> 00:09:30,130
What if she thinks
I'm pushing my luck?!

171
00:09:27,420 --> 00:09:30,130
<i>It's much harder to do this for idle talk!</i>

172
00:09:36,510 --> 00:09:39,110
Screw it!

173
00:09:39,470 --> 00:09:42,440
<i>Don't chicken out! Don't chicken out!</i>

174
00:09:49,790 --> 00:09:53,310
I mean, she wouldn't be checking 
her phone at this exact moment.

175
00:09:53,310 --> 00:09:57,330
If she couldn't even answer the door, 
she must be really bu—

176
00:09:55,870 --> 00:09:57,330
Read

177
00:09:57,330 --> 00:09:58,790
...sy!

178
00:09:59,080 --> 00:10:00,750
Fast!!

179
00:09:59,130 --> 00:10:00,750
Read receipt!

180
00:10:01,000 --> 00:10:04,050
<i>Mizuhara checked it! Is she home?</i>

181
00:10:01,040 --> 00:10:08,210
Is she bored?

182
00:10:04,050 --> 00:10:06,240
<i>Wait, she could've checked it anywhere.</i>

183
00:10:06,240 --> 00:10:08,210
<i>And that doesn't even matter!</i>

184
00:10:08,210 --> 00:10:10,170
Read

185
00:10:10,530 --> 00:10:12,260
<i>Is she typing now?</i>

186
00:10:14,220 --> 00:10:16,180
Read

187
00:10:18,890 --> 00:10:21,600
Read

188
00:10:26,810 --> 00:10:29,320
Ichinose Chizuru

189
00:10:38,950 --> 00:10:41,200
Read

190
00:10:48,590 --> 00:10:50,280
I should take a bath!

191
00:10:48,880 --> 00:10:54,300
Not that
she can see

192
00:10:50,280 --> 00:10:54,300
Yeah, it'd gross her out if I just 
sat here waiting for her to reply!

193
00:10:50,630 --> 00:10:54,300
But I'm like
some kinda stalker

194
00:11:01,140 --> 00:11:03,850
Heya! Some yoga pamphlet addressed to you got delivered
to me instead. Should I slip it through your mail slot?

195
00:11:01,140 --> 00:11:03,850
Read

196
00:11:04,890 --> 00:11:06,310
gloom

197
00:11:09,730 --> 00:11:13,860
I guess she's really busy! 
Play rehearsals, maybe?

198
00:11:10,270 --> 00:11:12,480
She might have a backlog
of class assignments

199
00:11:13,860 --> 00:11:17,320
Well, duh. I rang her doorbell, 
and she couldn't even answer that!

200
00:11:15,030 --> 00:11:15,740
Time to sleep!

201
00:11:16,150 --> 00:11:17,320
Night!

202
00:11:20,280 --> 00:11:24,500
Or she might be sick! Hope she's okay!

203
00:11:25,050 --> 00:11:29,340
<i>Grown-ups say communication and 
romance are instant in this day and age.</i>

204
00:11:29,340 --> 00:11:32,020
<i>You can pay money to be 
a pretty girl's "boyfriend,"</i>

205
00:11:32,020 --> 00:11:34,340
<i>and you can be connected to 
your beloved in a few seconds.</i>

206
00:11:35,420 --> 00:11:39,560
<i>When, then, will this pain instantly pass?</i>

207
00:11:37,300 --> 00:11:40,720
Got it. Thanks for that.

208
00:11:40,630 --> 00:11:42,440
<i>After we came back from Hawaiians...</i>

209
00:11:42,440 --> 00:11:48,040
<i>Since November 25, 
two days after we kissed...</i>

210
00:11:42,890 --> 00:11:48,350
Got it. Thanks for that.

211
00:11:49,030 --> 00:11:51,330
Chi-chan, rehearsal's starting.

212
00:11:51,330 --> 00:11:52,690
Oh, sorry.

213
00:11:56,840 --> 00:12:00,490
<i>Even the super-wary Ruka-chan 
had nothing to worry about.</i>

214
00:12:00,900 --> 00:12:02,950
<i>Because, for a period of three months,</i>

215
00:12:03,260 --> 00:12:07,330
<i>I couldn't get in touch 
with Mizuhara once.</i>

216
00:12:07,960 --> 00:12:09,960
Rent-a-Girlfriend

217
00:12:13,040 --> 00:12:14,320
Yes?

218
00:12:15,910 --> 00:12:17,380
That's my master!

219
00:12:16,210 --> 00:12:17,380
Is that cosplay?!

220
00:12:17,690 --> 00:12:22,180
Are you a shut-in who hasn't bathed 
in two weeks for Halloween?

221
00:12:21,430 --> 00:12:22,180
Halloween was quite
a while ago, though

222
00:12:22,430 --> 00:12:24,800
Bahut dino se mulakat nahi!

223
00:12:22,430 --> 00:12:24,800
(Long time no see!)

224
00:12:24,800 --> 00:12:26,220
Oh, it's just you.

225
00:12:26,500 --> 00:12:30,130
You should stop acting like anyone other 
than Mizuhara-san is a disappointment.

226
00:12:26,520 --> 00:12:40,070
What do you mean,
"just" me?

227
00:12:30,130 --> 00:12:32,460
Th-That's not what I meant...

228
00:12:33,490 --> 00:12:35,980
Your face is as red as 
the Lal Qila, the Red Fort.

229
00:12:35,980 --> 00:12:38,000
What even is that?

230
00:12:37,150 --> 00:12:40,070
Bahut?

231
00:12:38,000 --> 00:12:40,070
I was away on a trip to India!

232
00:12:38,900 --> 00:12:40,070
For a month

233
00:12:40,900 --> 00:12:43,830
I'd love to chat, 
but I'm sleeping right now.

234
00:12:45,020 --> 00:12:45,990
Huh?

235
00:12:49,180 --> 00:12:50,340
Wha...

236
00:12:51,460 --> 00:12:53,290
Th-This is bad!

237
00:12:56,510 --> 00:13:00,130
Wh-What's wrong, Master? 
Did something happen with Mizuhara-san?

238
00:13:07,590 --> 00:13:11,030
Master!

239
00:13:07,850 --> 00:13:09,270
Hang in there!

240
00:13:09,650 --> 00:13:12,230
<i>I love him because he never 
forgets to feed me at least.</i>

241
00:13:15,470 --> 00:13:16,690
You kissed?!

242
00:13:18,970 --> 00:13:20,610
Y-Yeah...

243
00:13:21,000 --> 00:13:21,820
Wha...

244
00:13:21,820 --> 00:13:26,600
Then what are you doing here? 
Why aren't you buried in her bosom?!

245
